extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 114-140 (cache p115-p141, cache page = printed folio + 1). The O.C.C. is printed 114-116, read off the text layer; the ten bodies are printed 116-140, read off renders for their vessel rows and checked by book-reconcile (cache p141 is welded and was read only from a render). || HEADING: Cyborg Shocktroopers, Class: Full Conversion Heavy Cyborg, then Cyborg Shocktrooper O.C.C. (printed 114-115), under Cyborg O.C.C.s on printed 57. The O.C.C. states no M.D.C. of its own (M.D.C. by Location: varies with specific type), so the class carries men_of_arms and each variant carries its body''s mdc_base. || XP: the ladder headed Cyborg Shocktroopers on the Experience Tables, printed 6. The page misprints level 2 as 2,601 where level 1 ends at 2,500; 2501 is stored. || VARIANTS: the ten bodies of printed 57 and 116, as variants on one class, the catalog''s own mechanism for one skill list over several bodies. Each variant''s mdc_base is the body''s main body, its attribute_dice the printed Robotic P.S. and Bionic P.P., its horror_factor and bonuses the body''s own. Only unconditional bonuses are stored; the conditional ones are in the Conditional Bonuses by Body ability. An extra attack that comes from a permanent limb (the Tempest''s tail, the White Tiger''s tentacles, the Holocaust''s extra arms) is stored. || ASSASSIN AND MANTIS ATTACKS: the Assassin prints +2 melee attacks and says they take into account the boxing skill and the extra pair of arms; the class already grants Boxing, whose row adds its own attack, so 1 is stored. The Mantis prints +1 and says it takes into account the boxing skill and other features; none is stored for the same reason. || BODY SKILLS: the Avenging Angel and the Assassin print bonus skills Prowl (+15%) and Acrobatics (+5%), the Mantis Prowl (+5%) and Acrobatics (+5%) and +10% to climbing, the White Tiger +15% to climbing; stored as skills_additional and skill_overrides. The Assassin and the Mantis also list Boxing, which the O.C.C. already grants. || W.P. HEAVY WEAPONS is stored as W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons, a reading. || MOS: four skills at +15% from ONE of Communications, Espionage, Military or W.P., stored as four mos options. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits stored (text layer !D6xlOOO); 3D6x100 in tradeable goods and the 1,600-2,200 credit monthly salary are in GM Notes. || NOT A BODY: printed 41 describes a Black Panther in Warlord Kolodenko''s write-up. It is a secret Heavy Machine, not a Shocktrooper, in one prose paragraph with no M.D.C. by Location and no weapon statistics; it is not a variant and has no vessel row."
---

## Lore

Shocktroopers are the Warlords'' elite: volunteers from loyal families who are
rebuilt into towering war machines with little or nothing human left to see.
Each Warlord fields his own design, and no one copies another''s. The last
two attempts ended in open war.

They rank just below the War-Knights and are, without argument, the biggest
and strongest things in a War Camp. To prove they are also the bravest they
take the worst assignments and lead the charge. Russian society honors them
for it, which is a large part of why minds housed in such bodies stay sound.

Among themselves they are a brotherhood. They fight side by side, carry
their fallen off the field even in a rout, and treat a wrecked body as a
comrade who may still be alive inside it.

## GM Notes

Pick the body as the variant; it must be the design of the Warlord the
character served. The variant gives the main body M.D.C., robotic P.S.,
bionic P.P., Horror Factor and unconditional bonuses. Everything else about
the body, the M.D.C. by location, speeds, weapon systems and Warlord cost, is
on its vessel row, named in the restrictions.

Pick one Military Specialty at creation: four skills from a single category
(Communications, Espionage, Military or W.P.), each at +15%.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: all the ammunition and equipment
for the body''s weapon systems and one weapon with four extra E-Clips for each
W.P. Maintenance and repairs are free in a Warlord''s service. Money is
1D6x1000 credits plus 3D6x100 in tradeable goods; pay is 1,600-2,200 credits
a month by rank and record. A cyborg jet pack, explosives, transport and more
weapons may be issued by assignment.

Running speeds, for reference: Tempest 70 mph, Butcher 120, Ripper 90, White
Tiger 144, Holocaust 80, Aftermath 100, Avenging Angel 70 with wings and 130
without, Assassin 110, Mantis 120, Demonfist 50. The Tempest and the
Avenging Angel fly.

A Shocktrooper who has left his Warlord on good terms still trades with,
warns and sometimes fights beside his old camp. One who left as a traitor or
deserter is harassed or attacked by old teammates on sight, and hunted in
earnest if he opposes them openly.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cyborg-shocktrooper');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cyborg-shocktrooper';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-cyborg-shocktrooper-class.sql');
